BeastieMon — lightweight FreeBSD system monitoring daemon.

Collects CPU, memory, disk I/O, network, filesystem, temperature, load,
and top-process metrics every second — plus optional ZFS pool/ARC and
jail panels — and serves them through a self-contained web dashboard
with live graphs (uPlot), a Prometheus /metrics exporter, and a
command-line tool (beastie) that samples standalone or reads the
running daemon (--remote), including a nagios-style check mode.

Optional SQLite history widens the dashboard beyond the in-memory hour
(tiered to hourly roll-ups past a week); optional threshold alerts POST
webhooks (raw/Slack/Discord), with a sampler watchdog, a rule-state API
(/api/alerts), and an Alerts dashboard card.

Authentication is optional (HTTP Basic and/or a bearer token, off by
default) and there is no TLS: bind to localhost and proxy through
nginx/haproxy for LAN or TLS access.

